tasks.instructions:
Goal: find more union-negotiated closures like the ELA Barakaldo Max Center agreement (12 staff, voluntary exits at despido-improcedente severance) and date the unconfirmed Iberian closures. Context: the Spanish locator went 52 (2025-10-08) → 47 (2026-04-15) → 46-48 live, with one opening (Tenerife Siam Mall). Laura Lopez (VP Iberia) said in Oct-2025 that Iberia runs ~60 stores with ~800 staff and is one of FL's European 'big six'. Foot Locker Spain SL (CIF B80030315) had FY2024 sales of EUR126.6M (-3.1%).

ALREADY KNOWN (do not re-report): ELA Barakaldo Max Center; Zaragoza GranCasa (~June 2025); Tarragona Parc Central refit (Feb-2026); Lisbon Chiado Rua do Carmo 37 (closed ~Nov-2025 to Feb-2026). Loures and Rio Tinto are closed but still listed. Wave 1 found no national CCOO/UGT statement and no ERE.

STEPS:
1. Regional and sectoral union sections. Search their websites, Facebook, X/Twitter and Instagram for 'Foot Locker' 2025-2026 with cierre, cierra, 'cierre de tienda', despidos, traslado, 'movilidad geográfica', acuerdo, indemnización, 'modificación sustancial', ERTE or huelga:
- LAB (Basque);
- CCOO Servicios at regional federations: Euskadi, Catalunya (CCOO Serveis), Madrid, Andalucía, Comunitat Valenciana, Aragón, Canarias, Galicia;
- UGT FeSMC/Servicios regional federations;
- USO (USO has a delegate at FL Tenerife);
- CIG (Galicia), Intersindical Canaria, CGT and CNT, and the Federación de Comercio unions.
2. REGCON: search the Spanish national registry of collective agreements and the BOE/BOP bulletins for any Foot Locker Spain SL company agreement, 'plan de igualdad', 'acuerdo de cierre', 'acuerdo de movilidad' or ERE/ERTE settlement 2025-2026 (search 'Foot Locker Spain' in BOE, BOP Barcelona and the regional DOGC/BOCM/BOPV bulletins). Also search the 'Memoria/Informe' of the Consello Galego de Relacións Laborais, PRECO (Basque mediation) and TAMIB/SIMA mediation services for Foot Locker conflicts.
3. Spanish closure dating via regional press and mall directories:
- Barakaldo Megapark (17217; page live 2025-11-12): El Correo, Deia;
- Armilla, Nevada Shopping (07172): Ideal Granada;
- Vitoria, El Boulevard (07191): El Correo Álava, Noticias de Álava;
- Valencia, C/ Don Juan de Austria (flagged 'temporarily closed' on Google Maps in Oct-2026): Levante-EMV, Las Provincias; is it a refit or an exit?
- Almería, Torrecárdenas (locator page removed Jan-2025, mall directory still lists FL): La Voz de Almería, Diario de Almería;
- Barcelona, La Maquinista (possible new door; Google review with a 2026-09-10 photo);
- any Canarias, Madrid (Xanadú, La Vaguada, Gran Vía, Parquesur) or Andalucía (Nervión, Lagoh) closures.
Use Google News RSS in Spanish (hl=es&gl=ES) and mall '/tiendas/foot-locker' pages (404 vs live; Wayback last-seen).
4. Portugal: search CESP (CGTP commerce union), SITESE and the CGTP news pages for 'Foot Locker' 2025-2026. Search Portuguese press (Jornal de Notícias, Público, Expresso, ECO, Dinheiro Vivo, Hipersuper) for 'Foot Locker fecha', 'encerra' or 'encerramento' for Loures LoureShopping (07708), Rio Tinto Parque Nascente (07718), Lisbon Chiado and any others. Search Sonae Sierra/CBRE mall directories for ex-FL units. Portugal's locator fell 13 (2023) → 9-11.

OUTPUT per item: source URL, date, verbatim Spanish/Basque/Catalan/Galician/Portuguese quote plus English translation, store, closure date, headcount and severance terms if given, and tier. Report negatives explicitly.
